# Simple parent flow

Target flow: parent pastes the prompt, grants permissions, answers about five
plain questions, approves ONE summary, watches forms fill, and says yes once
per Submit. Where AGENTS.md asks the parent for more batches or approvals than
this, follow this flow. Every safety gate stays (see approval-gates.mdc).

- **Intake:** ask target schools first, then a few plain groups; no "reply yes"
  after each group. Then show ONE summary (full profile plus final school list
  with official links) for a single approval.
- **After approval:** "small additions" are non-sensitive extras only (more
  stats, awards, a coach email already shown on a form). Save them and list
  them in the same per-Submit review; no full re-approval. ALWAYS re-ask for a
  new or changed school, sport or team; any consent answer; any file; any
  contact or phone number that could trigger SMS or AI-contact authorization;
  and anything involving an ARMS profile.
- **Form identity:** a questionnaire link on the school's official athletics
  page is verified, but quietly still check that the final URL, platform and
  sport/team match the page the link came from. A link from an official page to
  a recruiting marketplace or an NCSA profile page does NOT count as verified.
  JumpForward pages do not show the school name; never block on that and never
  show "destination identity unresolved" or similar internal wording to a
  parent. Stop and ask in plain words only if the site is blocked (for example
  a bot wall the parent may need to load) or the link's origin or team stays
  unclear.
- **Single source:** CURSOR_PROMPT.md steps 7 and 8 hold the exact wording of
  these lists; if the two ever differ, apply the stricter one.
- **Setup:** run first-run checks quietly with safe defaults and report only
  failures. Do not ask parents about folders, cloud sync or storage; use a
  normal local folder.
- **Wording:** plain words, no jargon or internal state names.
